          "id": "http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416",
          "type": "Type",
          "_label": "Details (Official List Description)"
        }
      ],
      "content": "BOVINGDON             \tHIGH STREET TL 0103 \t\t\t\t\t(South end)                                         10/29                                   \tThe Ryder Memorial 15.4.75 GV                                      \tII Wellhouse. 1881. By W. White FSA for Ryder family. Timber frame on red brick  plinth  with  blue  brick  chamfered  offsets.  Steep  pyramidal shingled roof. A small 5-sided timber structure in Medieval style. Moulded wooden corner piers with curved braces up to eaves - the whole structure open,  on an oak sill and chamfered brick plinth. Wooden shingle pyramidal roof with wrought iron finial. Bears the following inscription on wallplate:  'This house with its well dedicated to ye beloved memory/of ye Honble Granville D Ryder, late of Westbrook Hay in this Parish/he was born November 26th AD 1799/and died 24th November 1879/was raised by his relations for/the use and comfort of his friends/ the Villagers of Bovingdon April AD 1881/Let them remember ye waters/that never fail S John IV 14'.  The well itself has been covered over. (VCH(1908)216: Roberts(1975)No.30). Listing NGR: TL0148903764"
    }
  ],
